# docs/ is excluded EXCEPT docs/db, which Foundry's self-observation reads:
# `observeFoundryRepositoryReality` compares the live schema against
# docs/db/schema.snapshot.sql, and baseline liveness reads the six baseline
# files beside it. A blanket `docs/` kept those out of the BUILD CONTEXT, so the
# Dockerfile's COPY of docs/db could not have worked either — the fix and the
# thing defeating it sat in two different files.
#
# Written as explicit sibling exclusions rather than `docs/` plus `!docs/db/`.
# The negation form is the documented idiom, but its behaviour after a whole
# directory has been excluded is exactly the kind of subtlety that fails
# silently in a build nobody watches, and this is 308K.
docs/architecture/
docs/audits/
